  "published": "2026-09-16T17:23:24.81Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.1 - CreatePhonemizer now teaches itself the ecosystem's own proper nouns (EcosystemNames), because a name the letter-to-sound rules guess wrong passes every automated check there is: it is not dropped, not unmapped, and every phoneme it emits is real and encodable, so coverage reports 100% while the voice says a different word. Only a listener catches it. MEASURED: \"Reachy\" came out as IPA r-i-EI-k-i (ree-AY-kee, three syllables, stress on a vowel the word does not contain) because English spells ch as /k/ often enough - ache, stomach, chrome - that a model learned from a dictionary reaches for it. A caller's own Define still overrides anything here. Behaviour is otherwise unchanged.",
